  <name>MSGA</name>
  <summary>Fast native Slack client</summary>
  <developer id="com.nisdos">
    <name>Nisdos</name>
  </developer>

  <description>
    <p>
      MSGA is an unofficial Slack client that starts in under a second, needs a fraction of the
      memory of the official app and uses no CPU while idle. It is native code from top to bottom:
      no Electron, no web view, no GUI toolkit.
    </p>
    <p>Everything you expect from Slack works:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Channels, direct messages and threads</li>
      <li>Reactions, custom emoji, files, images and GIFs</li>
      <li>Notifications and a tray icon with unread counts</li>
      <li>Several workspaces side by side</li>
      <li>Sign-in with your browser session, or with your own Slack app for live updates</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      MSGA can also show your Claude Code sessions next to your workspaces, each one as a direct
      message: read them, answer them and start new ones, on this computer or on a server over
      ssh. Claude Code itself is not included; MSGA uses the one installed on your system.
    </p>
    <p>
      MSGA is not affiliated with, endorsed by or sponsored by Slack Technologies or Salesforce.
    </p>
  </description>

